---
import ImplementationSupport from './ImplementationSupport.astro';
import DocumentationLayout from '../../layouts/DocumentationLayout.astro';
import PreviewControls from './PreviewControls.astro';
import HeroBlockPreview from './HeroBlockPreview.astro';
import {CodeSnippet} from '../dmf-ui/code-block';
import {blocks} from '../../data/blocks';
import catalog from '../../../contracts/catalog.json';
const block=blocks.find(b=>b.slug==='hero')!,record=catalog.blocks.find(b=>b.slug==='hero')!,react=catalog.react.blocks.find(b=>b.name==='HeroBlock')!;
---
<DocumentationLayout title="HeroBlock" description={block.description} section="blocks" crumbs={[{name:'Blocks',href:'/blocks/'},{name:'HeroBlock'}]} toc={[{id:'preview',title:'Live preview'},{id:'usage',title:'Usage'},{id:'api',title:'API and composition'},{id:'behavior',title:'Responsive behavior'},{id:'acceptance',title:'Acceptance'}]}>
 <h1>HeroBlock</h1><p class="docs-lead">{block.description}</p><ImplementationSupport slug={'hero'} kind="block"/>
 <section id="preview" class="docs-section"><h2>Live preview</h2><PreviewControls/><HeroBlockPreview/></section>
 <section id="usage" class="docs-section"><h2>Usage</h2><p>Import the shared styles once and render inside a .dmf-ui scope. Actions and media are authored content, not generated from a service or a router configuration.</p><CodeSnippet code={block.usage} language="astro" title="Astro HeroBlock" wrap/><CodeSnippet code={`import {HeroBlock} from '@dmf-ui/react';\nimport '@dmf-ui/react/styles.css';\n\n<HeroBlock id="intro" title="Your authored page title"\n  actions={<a href="/docs/architecture/">Read composition guide</a>}\n/>`} language="tsx" title="React HeroBlock" wrap/></section>
 <section id="api" class="docs-section docs-prose"><h2>API and composition</h2><p>id and a nonempty title are required. headingLevel defaults to h1 and accepts h1/h2; choose h2 when a page already has its main heading. eyebrow and description are optional. layout is centered by default or split; mediaPosition is end by default or start. Native section attributes, class/style and React section refs remain available.</p><p>Astro composes Section and Text with actions/media/default slots. Use existing Button and Image in the slots when appropriate. React composes native section and Text with actions/media props and children. Supply native anchors or your application link component; the existing React Button keeps its native-button API. No new Section, image loader or polymorphic Button adapter is introduced.</p><p>Empty actions/media wrappers are omitted. Media is rendered before the copy for start and after it for end, preserving DOM order at every width. Hosts own alt text, dimensions, loading priority, video controls and failure fallback. Neither adapter creates autoplay, fetching, tracking or a loading state.</p><CodeSnippet code={record.declaration} language="ts" title="Astro Props" wrap/><CodeSnippet code={react.types[0].declaration} language="ts" title="React Props" wrap/><div class="docs-table-scroll"><table class="docs-options"><thead><tr><th>Property</th><th>Astro default</th></tr></thead><tbody>{Object.entries(record.defaults).map(([key,value])=><tr><td><code>{key}</code></td><td><code>{String(value)}</code></td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div></section>
 <section id="behavior" class="docs-section docs-prose"><h2>Responsive behavior and accessibility</h2><p>The section is a labelled region associated with its authored heading and optional description. Links remain native keyboard destinations; no focus controller or client initialization is needed. Do not place essential copy only inside media.</p><p>Split uses two equal columns only when the section container reaches 44rem and media is supplied. Narrow containers stack in source order even on a wide desktop. Centered stays one column; media-free split remains one column. Logical spacing supports RTL, natural action sizing and wrapping. Standard RTL does not change text size; enlarged text is a separate acceptance case.</p><p>Typography and gaps use the existing foundation scale. Brand scope is separate from layout. Nova/Neutral is the default. DMF light/dark and light-only HUI/QDI/CB retain their current boundaries. White HUI/CB primary action labels preserve the documented contrast exceptions.</p></section>
 <section id="acceptance" class="docs-section docs-prose"><h2>Dependencies and acceptance</h2><p>{block.limitations}</p><p>The existing packed Astro and React consumers exercise public imports, replaceable content, heading associations, media/action composition, DOM order and independent instances. Browser evidence remains scoped; no current Safari, Firefox, spoken-reader or physical-device HeroBlock acceptance is implied. This is an experimental source-owned Block, not a Template or registry installer.</p><p>Sources: <code>{record.source}</code> and <code>{react.source}</code>. <a href="/docs/architecture/">Architecture and responsive conventions</a>.</p></section>
</DocumentationLayout>
